    "Healthy Eating %@ · MIT License" : {

    },
    "Healthy Eating app icon" : {

    },
    "Healthy Eating can smooth your weigh-ins into a trend and estimate how many calories you maintain at, using your own log." : {

    },
    "Healthy Eating compares what you logged with what your weight did over the last 4 weeks.\n\nIt takes the average calories of the days that count for your averages, and the change of your smoothed weight trend over the same weeks. About 7,700 kcal match one kilogram of body weight. If the trend went down, you used more than you logged; if it went up, less.\n\nBecause it uses your own log, a steady over- or underestimate in it is part of both sides, so the result fits your log. It needs at least 14 logged days and weigh-ins on 6 days spread over 2 weeks. More days and more weigh-ins give a higher confidence.\n\nThe trend smooths day-to-day changes in weight, which come mostly from water and food, not from body tissue." : {

    },
    "Healthy Eating for iOS" : {

    },
    "Healthy Eating gets your meals from the chat you already use. Add this URL to Claude as a connector or to ChatGPT as a plugin." : {

    },
    "Healthy Eating is the app plus a PostgreSQL database on any server you control. Setup takes about 15 minutes." : {

